## Design check by prototype

I wrote the target Step 2 block to the plan's rules in a scratch directory. It has no functions and no positional parameters, uses logical `cd` for `APP_DIR` and `cd -P` for the root comparisons, and checks for exactly three levels below `cache`. I ran all 13 planned cases under dash (`/bin/sh` here), bash and busybox sh. Every case gave the planned `OWNER` and `APP_DIR`:

- Cases 1, 2, 3 and 10 gave `claude`. Cases 6 and 7 gave `cursor`. Cases 4, 5, 8 and 9 gave `dev`. Cases 11, 12 and 13 gave an empty `OWNER`.
- Case 9 (the mirror) gave the logical mirror `APP_DIR`, and its realpath is `<repo>/skills/sr-search`.

I also checked the Claude Code docs ([plugin loading](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/loading)). `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR` replaces the whole plugins root, and copies still go to `<root>/cache/<marketplace>/<plugin>/<version>/`. So case 3 models the custom root correctly. The installs on this machine have that shape in both harnesses. The warehouse shows Cursor agents running `sr-initialize` from `~/.cursor/plugins/cache/…`, never from `~/.cursor/plugins/marketplaces/…`.

